1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,283
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,277
Robotics 101, video 14.

3
00:00:06,327 --> 00:00:08,880
The final challenge.

4
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:13,515
You have built it, programmed it and tuned it.

5
00:00:13,565 --> 00:00:17,030
Now it is time to show what your robot can do.

6
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:22,906
Your challenge track has a start, some gentle curves, an S-bend, at

7
00:00:22,956 --> 00:00:27,305
least one sharp corner, and a black finish line across the track

8
00:00:27,355 --> 00:00:29,230
where the robot should stop.

9
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:34,828
Here is a full run in the simulator with pivot turns.

10
00:00:34,878 --> 00:00:39,320
Smooth, steady, and on the line all the way to the end.

11
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:48,063
There are three ways to hand in your project.

12
00:00:48,113 --> 00:00:52,576
If you built it, add a photo, your code and a video link.

13
00:00:52,626 --> 00:00:56,615
If your teacher watched it run, choose that option.

14
00:00:56,665 --> 00:01:02,870
If you have no kit, finish the S-curve and sharp-turns tracks in the simulator.

15
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:07,057
Your teacher looks at four things.

16
00:01:07,107 --> 00:01:09,998
Does it follow the line to the end?

17
00:01:10,048 --> 00:01:13,444
Does it handle the curves and the corner?

18
00:01:13,494 --> 00:01:15,041
Is your code clean?

19
00:01:15,091 --> 00:01:18,570
And can you explain one problem you fixed?

20
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:25,067
After your teacher approves it, take the final assessment to earn your

21
00:01:25,117 --> 00:01:28,684
certificate and the Line-Follower Champion badge.

22
00:01:28,734 --> 00:01:30,160
Well done, engineer!

23
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,875
Let us recap.

24
00:01:32,925 --> 00:01:36,643
Complete the track from start to finish.

25
00:01:36,693 --> 00:01:42,389
Hand in a photo, your code and a video, or use the simulator.

26
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:44,650
Your teacher reviews it.

27
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:49,360
Next: The final assessment, then your certificate.
